<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Eighth Dynasty of Egypt</h1><p class="st-meta">2181 BCE – 2160 BCE (approx.) · capital Memphis</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last Memphite kings after the collapse of the Old Kingdom, a dynasty of many brief reigns at the start of the First Intermediate Period.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the long reign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepi-ii">Pepi II</a> and the end of the Sixth Dynasty, a line of kings at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/memphis-egypt">Memphis</a> claimed to continue the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/old-kingdom-of-egypt">Old Kingdom of Egypt</a> around 2181 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manetho">Manetho's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seventh-dynasty-of-egypt">Seventh Dynasty</a>, of 'seventy kings in seventy days', is now usually regarded as fictitious, and its kings are counted with the Eighth.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/abydos">Abydos</a> king list names around a dozen or more rulers in roughly twenty years, most known only by name. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qakare-ibi">Qakare Ibi</a> built a small pyramid at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saqqara">Saqqara</a> inscribed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyramid-texts">Pyramid Texts</a>, and decrees of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neferkauhor">Neferkauhor</a> found at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coptos">Coptos</a> show royal favour granted to a powerful local family. Real power was passing to provincial governors, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> floods appear to have been low.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 2160 BCE the Memphite line was displaced by rulers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herakleopolis-magna">Herakleopolis</a>, who founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/herakleopolitan-kingdom">Herakleopolitan Kingdom</a>. Its brief, obscure history marks the end of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/old-kingdom-of-egypt">Old Kingdom</a> unity and the beginning of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-intermediate-period">First Intermediate Period</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 2181 BCE – 2160 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:16.30%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>2181 BCE – 2160 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/22nd-century-bce">22nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Memphis</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Qakare Ibi, Neferkauhor</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Egyptian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Egyptian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/egypt">Egypt</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Seventh and Eighth Dynasties, Memphite Eighth Dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-2170&amp;focus=eighth-dynasty-of-egypt" aria-label="Eighth Dynasty of Egypt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5493 1088 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Eighth Dynasty of Egypt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5813 1344L5813 1344M5813 1344L5807 1370"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5813 1344h0M5807 1370h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5813 1344h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5813 1344h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Memphis. <a href="/atlas?year=-2170&amp;focus=eighth-dynasty-of-egypt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
